<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ebro River</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Ebro</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ebro is a major river of north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, flowing into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a>. At its height the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almoravid-empire">Almoravid Empire</a> stretched from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/senegal-river">Senegal River</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-africa">West Africa</a> to the Ebro, marking the northern limit of its territory in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-andalus">al-Andalus</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ebro-river.jpg" alt="Ebro River" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Владимир Шеляпин · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Zaragoza_shel.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
